{{Repair Guide|Device=iPhone 16 Pro, iPhone 16 Pro Max|Affects parts=Main Logic Board|Needs equipment=Soldering iron, Hot Air Station, Microscope, Tweezer|Difficulty=4. Specialist|Type=Soldering}}

== Problem description ==

An iPhone 16 Pro/Max presented with persistent bootlooping on the Apple logo. Standard fixes such as flashing firmware and replacing the battery did not resolve the issue. Further board-level diagnostics revealed a failure on the Analog_BATT_VCELL_POS_CONN line traced back to the U4200 USB/Charging IC. Replacing the IC successfully restored functionality.
[[File:Stuck on logo.png|thumb|apple logo bootloop]]

== Symptoms ==

* Device stuck bootlooping on Apple logo
* Device does not charge when connected to power
* Occasionally boots up normally but remains unstable

== Diagnostic Steps ==

# Replace Battery – Installed a known-good battery (no improvement).
# Flash iOS – Attempted restore/flash in DFU and Recovery mode (device still bootloops).
# Measure Battery Connector – Found Analog_BATT_VCELL_POS_CONN line showing OL (open line).[[File:Batt fpc OL.png|center|thumb|battery fpc OL]]
# Trace Line – Followed the line from battery connector through PCB layers:
#* OL present even on lower PCB layers → rules out board-layer damage.
#* Only other connection point is U4200 USB/Charging IC.

[[File:U4200 ic board.png|center|thumb|u4200 ic]]

== Repair Steps ==

# Remove logic board and isolate U4200 IC area.
# Apply flux and controlled hot air rework to safely remove U4200.
# Clean pads and inspect for pad damage or corrosion.
# Install new U4200 USB/Charging IC with proper alignment.
# Reflow and allow the board to cool, then inspect solder joints.
# Reassemble device partially for testing.
# Re-measure Analog_BATT_VCELL_POS_CONN at battery connector:
#* Reading returned to normal continuity.
# Boot test – Device powers on normally, no more bootlooping.
# [[File:Phone on.png|center|thumb|phone successfully booted up to homescreen]]Finalize assembly, perform full charging and stability tests.